  "reproduction": {
    "real_defect": "Current implementation publishes only last FIFO cutoff when multiple MMC STOPs are dropped at distinct overflow boundaries while ISR refills a freed slot. First STOP is lost, last STOP executes after later PLAY.",
    "steps": "enqueue 16 PLAY messages from one SMC User MMC source; overflow STOP1 at w=16; after consumer releases first slot, enqueue PLAY17 then overflow STOP2 at w=17; compare event order.",
    "before_expected": "six GCC/Clang plain/UBSan/ASan+UBSan source-extracted runs exit 1, FAIL count 18 instead of 19 (17 PLAY, one STOP),",
    "after_expected": "16 original PLAY, STOP1, PLAY17, STOP2 (19 events), preserving phase and source ordering",
    "fix": "Replace single latest-cutoff generation with SPSC FIFO of 32 8-bit cutoff records per source. Deduplicate repeated STOPs at identical cutoff, retire STOP FIFO entry before executing callback. Project drop discards pending stop records. A 16-slot event ring admits at most 17 distinct cutoffs simultaneously."
  },
